The docstring states that this retries on "mid-stream EOFs". However, `r.do(ctx)` only performs the HTTP RoundTrip, returning as soon as response headers are read. Mid-stream EOFs occur during the reading of the response body (`resp.Body.Read`), which is handled by the caller of `doWithRetries` or `doWithRetriesInner`. Consequently, any mid-stream EOF will not be visible to `doWithTransportRetries` and will not trigger a retry under this implementation. It is safer to correct the docstring to prevent misleading future engineers about the capabilities of this retry loop.

